[[backlinks]]
Backlinks: who references a symbol

A backlink query returns every call site or reference that points at a given symbol.
Where impact analysis looks outward to what a change reaches, backlinks look inward
to who depends on the symbol right now — the immediate callers and the places that
name it. It is the graph equivalent of an editor's find-all-references, but it works
from a symbol name rather than a cursor position in an open file.

Backlinks are the first thing to consult before renaming or deleting a symbol,
because they enumerate the exact sites that must be updated. They are direct by
definition: a backlink is a one-hop edge into the symbol, not the multi-hop transitive
closure that a downstream impact walk produces.
